  "response_text": "A system call is how a program requests a hardware specific function that is controlled by the OS. It is needed because programs run in user mode, which has very limited functions. As such, the program wants to perform a privileged function, such as reading from a file, it generates a system call to ask (or \u201cinterrupt\u201d) the OS, since the OS runs in kernel mode and has full access to the system.\\n",
